  "label": "Settler colonialism",
  "description": "A form of colonialism in which settlers establish permanent settlements in a territory, often displacing or eradicating indigenous populations, and imposing their own cultural, political, and economic systems. This concept underpins the historical context of 'white settler' and is central to critiques of cultural appropriation in colonized contexts.",
